        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "whose Hessian is  $ \\mathbf{H}_F = 2\\mathbf{X}_F\\mathbf{X}_F^\\top $, where  $ F $ denotes the set of remaining full-precision weights, the greedy-optimal weight to quantize next, which we denote by  $ w_q $, and the corresponding optimal update of all weights in  $ F $, denoted by  $ \\delta_F $, are given by the following formulas, where  $  \\text{quant}(w)  $ rounds  $ w $ to the nearest value on the quantization grid:",
            "block_bbox": [
