        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "OBQ quantizes weights iteratively using these two equations, until all the weights of w are quantized. This is done efficiently, avoiding expensive full recomputations of  $ H^{-1} $, by removing the qth row and column of H, which is necessary after quantizing  $ w_q $, directly in the inverse via one step of Gaussian elimination. Namely, the updated inverse is given by the formula",
            "block_bbox": [
                210,
                328,
                1013,
                417
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
